From: BeatLink <pearson.pryce.p@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_battery: name the battery

Both batteries showed up unnamed in Settings, which made the phone's own
cell and the keyboard case's pack indistinguishable. UPower reads the model
from the sysfs model_name attribute, which this driver did not export.

Fork-specific: this driver also serves the axp209, axp221 and axp813, so the
name only holds because this tree builds for one device.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -311,6 +311,10 @@
 	int ret = 0, reg, val1;
 
 	switch (psp) {
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME:
+		val->strval = "PinePhone";
+		return 0;
+
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE:
 		ret = regmap_read(axp20x_batt->regmap, AXP20X_PWR_OP_MODE,
@@ -930,6 +934,7 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ENERGY_FULL_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ENERGY_EMPTY_DESIGN,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME,
 };
 
 static enum power_supply_property axp717_battery_props[] = {
